# Project 6: AWS IAM Password Policy

## Objective

Configure an **AWS IAM Password Policy** to enforce strong password requirements for IAM users and improve account security.

## Project Overview

In this project, I configured a custom password policy in AWS IAM to ensure that IAM users create strong and secure passwords.

The password policy was configured with requirements for minimum password length, uppercase letters, lowercase letters, numbers, and special characters.

This helps reduce the risk of weak passwords and unauthorized access.

## AWS Services Used

* AWS IAM
* AWS Management Console

## Password Policy Configuration

The following password requirements were configured:

| Security Requirement               | Configuration                               |
| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Minimum Password Length            | 14 characters                               |
| Require Uppercase Letters          | Enabled                                     |
| Require Lowercase Letters          | Enabled                                     |
| Require Numbers                    | Enabled                                     |
| Require Special Characters         | Enabled                                     |
| Allow IAM Users to Change Password | Enabled                                     |
| Password Expiration                | Configured according to project requirement |
| Password Reuse Prevention          | Configured according to project requirement |

## Password Requirements

IAM users must create passwords that satisfy the configured security requirements.

Example of the required structure:

```text
Minimum 14 characters
        +
Uppercase letter
        +
Lowercase letter
        +
Number
        +
Special character
```

Example format:

```text
StrongPassword@2026
```

> Never use this example as an actual AWS password.

